# fixedbugs, defect 570, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R1).
#
# Beside `fixedbugs-570-an-integer-for-a-pointer-is-refused-through-the-pragma`,
# the row through a library's own declaration (panel 205's `icv`).
#
# SYMPTOM: through a header writing `#pragma clang diagnostic ignored
# "-Wint-conversion"` before `#include <string.h>`, `strlen(s: i64)`
# against `size_t strlen(const char *)` built at exit 0.
#
# FIX: after the groups' includes, and again at the probe region, every
# warning a check of a binding rests on is raised again
# (`emit/checks_raised.hero`), the build's `-Werror` words and clang's three
# default errors, so the message is the one a plain header gets.

extern "fixedbugs-570-an-integer-for-a-library-s-pointer-is-refused-through-the-pragma.h"
    function strlen(s: i64) -> u64  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    print(strlen(0))
